#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:37
msgid "The arguments of `update_hbm()` map onto these names. Both functions refit from scratch, as `brms::update()` reruns `brm()`:"
msgstr "Argumen `update_hbm()` dipetakan ke nama-nama berikut. Kedua fungsi melakukan fitting ulang dari awal, seperti `brms::update()` yang menjalankan ulang `brm()`:"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "R `update_hbm(...)`"
msgstr "R `update_hbm(...)`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "Python `update_model(...)`"
msgstr "Python `update_model(...)`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`object`"
msgstr "`object`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`model`"
msgstr "`model`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`newdata = df`"
msgstr "`newdata = df`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`new_data=df`"
msgstr "`new_data=df`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`formula. = . ~ . + x2`"
msgstr "`formula. = . ~ . + x2`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`formula=\". ~ . + x2\"`"
msgstr "`formula=\". ~ . + x2\"`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`prior = ...` (through `...`)"
msgstr "`prior = ...` (melalui `...`)"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`priors={...}`, merged into the current priors"
msgstr "`priors={...}`, digabungkan ke prior saat ini"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`iter = 4000, warmup = 2000`"
msgstr "`iter = 4000, warmup = 2000`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`draws=2000, tune=2000` (`iter` includes warm-up, `draws` does not)"
msgstr "`draws=2000, tune=2000` (`iter` termasuk warm-up, `draws` tidak)"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`chains`, `cores`"
msgstr "`chains`, `cores`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`control = list(adapt_delta = 0.99)`"
msgstr "`control = list(adapt_delta = 0.99)`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`target_accept=0.99`"
msgstr "`target_accept=0.99`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`control = list(max_treedepth = 12)`"
msgstr "`control = list(max_treedepth = 12)`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`max_treedepth=12`"
msgstr "`max_treedepth=12`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`seed = 1` (through `...`)"
msgstr "`seed = 1` (melalui `...`)"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`random_seed=1`"
msgstr "`random_seed=1`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:52
msgid "R returns a new `hbmfit` and leaves the original unchanged. `update_model()` updates the model in place and returns its new `ModelResult`."
msgstr "R mengembalikan `hbmfit` baru dan membiarkan yang asli tidak berubah. `update_model()` memperbarui model secara in-place dan mengembalikan `ModelResult` barunya."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:55
msgid "Pinned parameters"
msgstr "Parameter yang dipatok"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:57
msgid "`fixed_params` keeps its name. `sampling_variance` in R and `sampling_var=` here both mean `sigma = sqrt(D)`:"
msgstr "`fixed_params` tetap bernama sama. `sampling_variance` di R dan `sampling_var=` di sini sama-sama berarti `sigma = sqrt(D)`:"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`sampling_variance = \"D\"`"
msgstr "`sampling_variance = \"D\"`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`sampling_var=\"D\"`"
msgstr "`sampling_var=\"D\"`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`fixed_params = list(sigma = \"sd_col\")`"
msgstr "`fixed_params = list(sigma = \"sd_col\")`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`fixed_params={\"sigma\": \"sd_col\"}`"
msgstr "`fixed_params={\"sigma\": \"sd_col\"}`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`fixed_params = list(sigma = 2)`"
msgstr "`fixed_params = list(sigma = 2)`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`fixed_params={\"sigma\": 2.0}`"
msgstr "`fixed_params={\"sigma\": 2.0}`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`fixed_params = list(phi = ...)`"
msgstr "`fixed_params = list(phi = ...)`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`fixed_params={\"kappa\": ...}`"
msgstr "`fixed_params={\"kappa\": ...}`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`fixed_params = list(sigma = c(...))`"
msgstr "`fixed_params = list(sigma = c(...))`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "add the vector as a column, pass its name"
msgstr "tambahkan vektornya sebagai kolom, berikan namanya"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`fixed_params = list(phi = ~ I(n/deff - 1))`"
msgstr "`fixed_params = list(phi = ~ I(n/deff - 1))`"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:20
msgid "`n=`/`deff=`, or pre-compute a column"
msgstr "`n=`/`deff=`, atau hitung kolomnya lebih dulu"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:69
msgid "Three differences to watch:"
msgstr "Tiga perbedaan yang perlu diperhatikan:"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:71
msgid "**The Beta precision is `kappa`, not `phi`.** brms calls it `phi` and Bambi calls it `kappa`. The value is the same, `n/deff - 1`."
msgstr "**Presisi Beta bernama `kappa`, bukan `phi`.** brms menamainya `phi` dan Bambi menamainya `kappa`. Nilainya sama, `n/deff - 1`."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:74
msgid "**A vector or a one-sided formula becomes a column.** R accepts `c(...)` and `~ I(n/deff - 1)`. Here the value is a column name or a single number: compute it in pandas and pass the column name."
msgstr "**Vektor atau formula satu sisi menjadi kolom.** R menerima `c(...)` dan `~ I(n/deff - 1)`. Di sini nilainya berupa nama kolom atau satu angka: hitung di pandas lalu berikan nama kolomnya."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:78
#, python-format
msgid "**The pin is tight, not exact.** R writes `<par> ~ 0 + offset(...)`. Bambi 0.18 crashes on the empty design matrix, so hbsaemp writes `1 + offset(...)` and holds the intercept with a `Normal(0, 1e-3)` prior. The parameter lands within about 0.1% of the pinned value."
msgstr "**Pematokannya ketat, bukan eksak.** R menulis `<par> ~ 0 + offset(...)`. Bambi 0.18 crash pada matriks desain yang kosong, sehingga hbsaemp menulis `1 + offset(...)` dan menahan intersepnya dengan prior `Normal(0, 1e-3)`. Parameternya berada dalam kisaran sekitar 0,1% dari nilai yang dipatok."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:82
msgid "The dataset names and their column names are the same as in R:"
msgstr "Nama dataset dan nama kolomnya sama dengan di R:"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:96
msgid "Check it worked"
msgstr "Periksa hasilnya"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:98
msgid "Fit both versions on the same bundled dataset and compare the posterior summaries. They should agree relative to their standard errors, not digit for digit: the two packages use different samplers and seeds."
msgstr "Lakukan fitting kedua versi pada dataset bawaan yang sama dan bandingkan ringkasan posteriornya. Keduanya semestinya sepakat relatif terhadap galat bakunya, bukan digit demi digit: kedua paket memakai sampler dan seed yang berbeda."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:102
msgid "If it fails"
msgstr "Jika gagal"

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:104
msgid "These differences are deliberate."
msgstr "Perbedaan berikut disengaja."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:106
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Building and fitting are separate.** In R, `hbm()` fits. Here it returns an unfitted model and you call `fit()`. This lets you run {doc}`02-specify-model` and {doc}`03-check-priors` before any sampling."
msgstr "**Membangun dan melakukan fitting terpisah.** Di R, `hbm()` langsung melakukan fitting. Di sini fungsi itu mengembalikan model yang belum di-fit dan Anda memanggil `fit()`. Dengan begitu Anda dapat menjalankan {doc}`02-specify-model` dan {doc}`03-check-priors` sebelum sampling apa pun."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:121
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Sampler settings go in a config object.** Build a `ModelConfig` and pass it as `config=`. See {doc}`04-fit-model`."
msgstr "**Pengaturan sampler ditaruh di objek config.** Bangun sebuah `ModelConfig` dan berikan sebagai `config=`. Lihat {doc}`04-fit-model`."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:124
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**No transformations inside the formula.** R accepts `log(x)` and `x1:x2`. Here every term must be a column name, and anything else raises. Compute the column first, as {doc}`02-specify-model` shows."
msgstr "**Tidak ada transformasi di dalam formula.** R menerima `log(x)` dan `x1:x2`. Di sini setiap suku harus berupa nama kolom, dan selain itu memunculkan galat. Hitung kolomnya lebih dulu, seperti ditunjukkan {doc}`02-specify-model`."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:128
msgid "**Family-specific arguments are checked.** Passing `trials=` to a Gaussian model raises instead of being ignored."
msgstr "**Argumen khusus family diperiksa.** Memberikan `trials=` ke model Gaussian memunculkan galat alih-alih diabaikan."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:131
msgid "**The lognormal family is not available.** `data_lnln` loads, but `family=\"lognormal\"` raises a roadmap error."
msgstr "**Family lognormal belum tersedia.** `data_lnln` dapat dimuat, tetapi `family=\"lognormal\"` memunculkan galat peta jalan."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:134
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**WAIC is not available.** Model comparison uses PSIS-LOO-CV only. See {doc}`07-check-fit-and-compare`."
msgstr "**WAIC tidak tersedia.** Perbandingan model hanya memakai PSIS-LOO-CV. Lihat {doc}`07-check-fit-and-compare`."

#: ../../source/python/how-to/migrate-from-hbsaems.md:137
msgid "**The Bayes factor answers a different question.** In R, `comparison_metrics = \"bf\"` compares two whole models by bridge sampling. Here `metrics=[\"bf\"]` gives a Savage-Dickey Bayes factor for each coefficient of one model. To weigh two nested models, read the Bayes factor of the coefficient that separates them."
msgstr "**Faktor Bayes menjawab pertanyaan yang berbeda.** Di R, `comparison_metrics = \"bf\"` membandingkan dua model utuh melalui bridge sampling. Di sini `metrics=[\"bf\"]` memberikan faktor Bayes Savage-Dickey untuk setiap koefisien dari satu model. Untuk menimbang dua model bersarang, baca faktor Bayes dari koefisien yang membedakan keduanya."

